@startuml
' What: how the "most" picks of a generation become the era policy (D-44).
' Shows: lookup by family and fit (10 policy sets), fitting scaled by connections, additive stacking,
'        injection into Unciv's temporaryUniques until the next generation change.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-44, D-45, D-47, Appendix C, §4 Engine notes. Magnitudes are playtest values.
title From picks to era policy (D-44)
start
:Collect the "most" picks of this generation;
note right: held, dice-flipped and cancelled lines\nset no policy
:For each pick: family of the picked keyword\n+ fit (fitting / tempting);
:Look up the policy set (Appendix C, 10 sets);
if (fitting?) then (yes)
  :Scale by connections x connection factor\n(D-45, D-47), with a cap;
else (tempting)
  :Flat, immediate bonus, works alone;
endif
:Stack all policies additively;
:Fate engine replaces its entries in temporaryUniques\n(turnsLeft = -1, keyword as source name);
:Active until the next generation change;
stop
@enduml
